{
  "id": "Compound::DB01601 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Lopinavir is likely to interact with Cyp2c9 through a series of molecular and enzymatic pathways. The evidence suggests that Lopinavir binds to Cyp2b6, which then participates in the oxidation of arachidonic acid, either as an arachidonic acid monooxygenase or epoxygenase. Both of these activities are associated with Cyp2c9, indicating a potential functional link between Lopinavir and Cyp2c9. The shared participation in these enzymatic processes implies that Lopinavir may influence Cyp2c9 through a mechanism involving the modulation of arachidonic acid metabolism. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent and significant relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways involving Cyp2b6 and Cyp2c9 highlights the importance of these enzymes in the metabolic response to Lopinavir.",
